{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224782-scale-examples","id":1224782,"title":"Scale Examples","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-04T12:31:48-07:00","id":1224782,"title":"Scale Examples","content":"i'm trying to be confident with the scale but i'm still working on it<br /> <br /> in my last game the son of ares said (with epic strenght) &quot;i want to lift the car and throw it in front of me to stop the run of the troll&quot;<br /> <br /> Me: okay, you have a +1 scale because of epic strenght, i would say... 4 of difficulty because of the weight of the car, the rush of the moment and blablabla<br /> <br /> he throw the dices, 5 success x2, 10 successes<br /> <br /> He will do this with great style.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, my point is: in this case he had a +1 scale because of epic strenght<br /> <br /> But without epic strenght, i should let him do something cool like this giving him a +1 scale??<br /> <br /> what do you think?? in wich situation you would give a + scale?<br /> <br /> <br /> do you have some examples from your plays? or made up some examples to allowe me understand better the scale stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","user":"ElanConnor","date":". 06-06-2018, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-05T18:02:12-07:00","id":1225123,"title":"","content":"Whoa now, hold up...<br /> <br /> Scale 1 doesn't double your successes on a roll. It gives +2 Enhancement. So instead of 10 successes, he should have gotten 7.<br /> <br /> Which still aces it yes but still, something to keep in mind going forward","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T07:58:25-07:00","id":1225272,"title":"","content":"it depends on what scale you're using<br /> <br /> on narrative scale is x2 successes, on drama scale is +2 enhancements<br /> <br /> or am i totally misunderstood?<br /> <br /> Add:<br /> <br /> on manual says that lifting a car is 10 successess! are 7 successes okay to lift a car?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","user":"ElanConnor","date":". 06-06-2018, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T08:03:21-07:00","id":1225278,"title":"","content":"Sorry the double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","user":"ElanConnor","date":". 06-06-2018, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T08:09:00-07:00","id":1225280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElanConnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1224782-scale-examples?p=1225272#post1225272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it depends on what scale you're using<br /> <br /> on narrative scale is x2 successes, on drama scale is +2 enhancements<br /> <br /> or am i totally misunderstood?<br /> <br /> Add:<br /> <br /> on manual says that lifting a car is 10 successess! are 7 successes okay to lift a car?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you are correct but i think the problem is that your only really supposed to use the Narrative scale for trivial targets. Like when a giant stomps someone in a crowd, you use that scale. The Drama scale is when the players face off against enemies or story important characters. That's how I remember it's supposed to be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T08:42:58-07:00","id":1225295,"title":"","content":"oooh... i got it, so narrative is for trivial NPC and drama f